From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cinders of Chaos <noreply@cindersofchaos.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:07:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Render: skip the effect buffer when no effect is active

synchronize() collected the placement effect instances and rebuilt the
effect vertex staging on every frame, also when no effect was active: a
temporary vector, a QByteArray and a dirty mark per frame. The collection
now runs only while effects are active, plus one more frame to clear the
last one. Drawing is unchanged: an empty list was never drawn.
---
 editor/map/maprhiview.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/editor/map/maprhiview.cpp b/editor/map/maprhiview.cpp
index d35a82b..2d3a338 100644
--- a/editor/map/maprhiview.cpp
+++ b/editor/map/maprhiview.cpp
@@ -301,7 +301,9 @@ public:
         };
         if (m_previewWindow) {
             m_fxInst.clear(); m_fxCount = 0;
-        } else {
+        } else if (src->hasActiveEffects() || m_fxCount > 0) {
+            // Without active effects the collected list stays empty; skip the
+            // per-frame allocation and the dirty mark of an empty buffer.
             src->renderCollectEffectInstances(m_fxInst);
             uploadDyn(m_fxVbo, m_fxInst, m_fxCount);
         }
